# SleepAway — Driver Fatigue Detection & Prevention System

> A retrofittable, low-cost driver fatigue detection system for older vehicles.  
> University of Wollongong — Engineering Capstone Project 2025

---

## Overview

Driver fatigue is responsible for an estimated **20–30% of fatal and serious road crashes** in Australia (Australian Automobile Association). The average passenger vehicle on Australian roads is 11.4 years old, meaning the majority of drivers have no built-in fatigue detection system.

SleepAway is a two-module device that retrofits fatigue detection into any vehicle cheaply and easily — no installation required beyond a dashboard mount and USB power.

---

## System Architecture

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────┐     BLE 5       ┌──────────────────────────┐
│         Dashboard Module            │ ◄────────────►  │     Headband Module      │
│                                     │                 │                          │
│  Raspberry Pi 5 (2GB)               │                 │  ESP32-C3 Mini           │
│  XC9021 IR Camera (OV5647)          │                 │  MPU6050 IMU             │
│  Adafruit GPS Breakout v3           │                 │  Vibration motor         │
│  Grove Vision AI V2 (YOLO)          │                 │  1100mAh LiPo battery    │
│  3W LED + Gravity Speaker           │                 │  Makerverse USB-C charger│
└─────────────────────────────────────┘                 └──────────────────────────┘
```

---

## Detection Methods

### Vision AI — Dashboard Module
- **Primary:** MediaPipe Face Mesh (468 3D landmarks) with Eye Aspect Ratio (EAR) calculation
- **Secondary:** YOLOv8n on Grove Vision AI V2 Ethos-U55 NPU (experimental)
- **Fallback:** OpenCV Haar cascade + dlib 68 landmark detection

### IMU — Headband Module
- MPU6050 accelerometer + gyroscope
- Pitch angle calculation for head nod detection
- Digital Low Pass Filter (DLPF) at 10Hz — configured in firmware, no hardware filter needed

### GPS — Dashboard Module
- Speed variance monitoring over a rolling time window
- Erratic speed changes contribute to fatigue score

### Sensor Fusion
All three sources feed into a weighted fatigue score:

```
Score = F_camera × W_c  +  F_imu × W_i  +  F_gps × W_g

where W_c + W_i + W_g = 1  and  0 < F < 100
```

Camera is weighted heaviest, GPS lightest.

---

## Alert System

When the combined fatigue score exceeds the threshold:
- 🔴 **3W 200 lumen LED** flashes (GPIO17 via 2N2222 transistor)
- 🔊 **Speaker** plays a rising tone alert (GPIO18)
- 📳 **Vibration motor** pulses against the driver's head (ESP32 GPIO4)

